// fewer where it doesn't, never none:
//   SEC            G 46 · B 43
//   Big Ten        G 50 · B 48
//   Big 12         G 45 · B 38
//   ACC            G 54 · B 50
//   Big East       G 33 · B 32
//   Pac-12         G 26 · B 21
//   Mountain West  G 27 · B 24
//   American       G 35 · B 27
//   A-10           G 41 · B 35
//   WCC            G 26 · B 22
//   MVC            G 30 · B 22
// COLLEGE legends: picked and graded on what they did in college (national players of the year, All-Americans, Final
// Four stars, the school's record holders), not on their NBA careers. The lists were checked against each school's
// consensus All-Americans and season leaderboards (sports-reference.com/cbb school pages).
// honors: from his sports-reference record (awards, All-America teams, titles, career numbers). years: his seasons.
//
// ── Grades ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 769 of 775 are graded from their researched college record (season and career numbers, awards, listed
// height and weight). Each trait is its own evidence weighed with a style grade: Jump Shot from three-point and
// free-throw accuracy and volume for his era (free throws, field-goal accuracy and scoring before the 1986-87 line);
// Finishing from two-point accuracy against his era, free throws drawn and scoring; Passing/Playmaking from assists;
// Rebounding from rebounds a game scaled for his era's pace; defense from steals, blocks and defensive awards (where
// they were kept); Basketball IQ and Leadership/Clutch from All-America teams, player-of-the-year awards, titles and
// tournament honors; Speed, Bounce and Handles from how he played (style grades: no box score records them); Size
// from height and weight (a small guard is small, and nothing else on his card pays him back for it). No tier fit.
// The one calibration is a résumé lift that moves a whole card evenly (never one trait more than another): none for
// an all-conference player, up to one grade for the sport's inner circle; it never makes an S.
// Guards: median 87, middle half 85-91, 3 at 99, 26 at 95+. Bigs: median 87, middle half 85-91, 8 at 99, 31 at 95+.
// Photos: ESPN only (189): the game's own NBA headshot where he is in the NBA pools ('nba/…'), else ESPN's
// headshot of him (cbbl_ an NBA photo, cbb_ a college one). No ESPN photo: the school's logo.
